From 80471b0ad66a725e51f517bbfe70ee6f4b5fb38a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Daniel Campos Ramos <Capitain_Jack@yahoo.com>
Date: Wed, 7 Oct 2026 13:57:42 -0300
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] Do not activate a button twice on Return

Bigscreen.Button handles Return itself (it calls click()), and MenuButton and
OSDButton handled it as well, so a press of Return on the OSD or in a menu
emitted clicked() twice: the play/pause button paused and resumed at once,
and any toggle in a menu was undone. Leave it to Bigscreen.Button.

Assisted-by: Claude Sonnet via Claude Code
---
 app/qml/MenuButton.qml | 4 ----
 app/qml/OSDButton.qml  | 4 ----
 2 files changed, 8 deletions(-)

diff --git a/app/qml/MenuButton.qml b/app/qml/MenuButton.qml
index e066b92..1d1ffe8 100644
--- a/app/qml/MenuButton.qml
+++ b/app/qml/MenuButton.qml
@@ -22,8 +22,4 @@ Bigscreen.Button {
         }
         return null;
     }
-
-    Keys.onReturnPressed: (event)=> {
-        clicked()
-    }
  }
diff --git a/app/qml/OSDButton.qml b/app/qml/OSDButton.qml
index 95b4726..9de1e54 100644
--- a/app/qml/OSDButton.qml
+++ b/app/qml/OSDButton.qml
@@ -26,8 +26,4 @@ Bigscreen.Button {
             color: osdBtn.checked ? Kirigami.Theme.negativeTextColor : Kirigami.Theme.textColor
         }
     }
-
-    Keys.onReturnPressed: (event)=> {
-        clicked()
-    }
  }
